ents":7,"created_at":"2024-12-05T03:03:51Z","updated_at":"2025-03-15T19:24:50Z","closed_at":"2024-12-05T20:16:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nJust synced mainline yesterday when I noticed this happening: v4.4.dev.custom_build [4497273fd]\nDidn't happen in 4.3 or 4.4-dev5.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev (4497273fd) - Windows 10.0.19045 - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6603) - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThere are certain locations where things will just get completely occluded, even though they're out in the open.  Seems to be random each run, so the locations where things occlude will change.  Here are a couple clips to demonstrate the issue:\n\nhttps://www.twitch.tv/jitspoe/clip/HeartlessTenuousCardAMPTropPunch-6opP9uinLWBMT6P1\nhttps://www.twitch.tv/jitspoe/clip/WittyCheerfulIcecreamSaltBae-9Q3UarksnpuI7fS4\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIt's difficult to reproduce consistently, as it seems random.  Never had it happen before I synced the latest main, though.  In my case, I used the bsp importer to import a medium complexity map with the occluder option enabled: https://godotengine.org/asset-library/asset/2147\n\nWhen walking around the level, sometimes lights and other objects would disappear.  Standing in specific locations would cause a bunch of things to stop rendering as though there were an occluder polygon just floating in space, there.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nStill trying to work out a way to consistently repro this in a MRP, but considering the severity of it for anybody using occluders, I thought I'd report it while I try to work out the details.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100032/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100032/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}